Ladybird parses a content script in the extension world’s realm
while the script keeps the document’s settings object, through
ClassicScript::create_in_realm(). WebKit does the equivalent in
LocalFrame::injectUserScriptImmediately(), which hands the source
to ScriptController::evaluateInWorldIgnoringException(source, world),
so the script compiles and runs against that world’s
JSDOMWindow while the frame’s own ScriptController owns the run.
Blink’s ScriptInjection::InjectJs() calls
WebLocalFrame::RequestExecuteScript(world_id, sources, …), which
compiles each source in the isolated world’s v8::Context of the
same frame. Gecko’s ExtensionContent.sys.mjs compiles a content
script as a Script bound to the sandbox and runs it with
executeInGlobal(sandbox), the sandbox being a separate global that
shares the content window as its prototype.
